\newlabel{fig:practice}{{6}{19}{}{figure.6}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {7}{\ignorespaces In this environment universality moves the drift and the verifier's error rate does not. Left: log-odds drift against universality, one line per false-positive rate. Right: the same data against the static false-positive rate, one line per universality, common $y$-scale. Varying accepted wrong responses per prompt from 1--8{} moves the false-positive rate over 1.0--8.1\%{} and mildly \emph  {reduces} hacking; universality moves the drift monotonically and much further.}}{19}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:factorial}{{7}{19}{}{figure.7}{}}
